# ANV-0040 -- the checker compared a log index against a machine without it
# TopologyMachine::applied_index() is the last index handed to apply(); a
# snapshot install hands over a whole state and no index at all
seed        = 4
workload    = shard_kv
nodes       = 5
faults      = drawn from seed; needs a snapshot install
invariant   = INV-SHARD-09 (it reported a divergence between two correct nodes)
reproduce   = anvil_shard_faults 8
note        = fixed twice over: the checker reads the Raft log's applied index,
              and RaftNode::snapshot_pending() lets it skip a node that is
              between the two. A checker that can invent a finding is worse than
              one that misses one.
found_at    = P5
fixed_at    = P5
